tcc-native-guard.patch - MayteraOS target adaptation for TinyCC tcc.h.

WHY. tcc.h derives TCC_IS_NATIVE from the host compiler predefining __x86_64__
(the cross gcc always does), so tcc would build as a NATIVE compiler with its
-run path: tccrun.c #includes <sys/mman.h> (absent in the MayteraOS freestanding
userland), maps executable memory, and installs a SIGSEGV/ucontext backtrace
handler; CONFIG_TCC_BCHECK is switched on too. None of that runtime exists here.
This patch adds "!defined MAYTERAOS &&" to the single #if that gates native
detection, so -DMAYTERAOS (in the recipe cflags) builds tcc as a CROSS-style
compiler that only writes files, with the -run machinery #ifdef-ed out.

A target adaptation, not a bug fix: the compiler source is otherwise byte-for-
byte unaltered, so there is no patch series to rot at the next version bump.

--- a/tcc.h
+++ b/tcc.h
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@
 #endif
 
 /* only native compiler supports -run */
-#if defined _WIN32 == defined TCC_TARGET_PE
+#if !defined MAYTERAOS && (defined _WIN32 == defined TCC_TARGET_PE)
 # if (defined __i386__ || defined _X86_) && defined TCC_TARGET_I386
 #  define TCC_IS_NATIVE
 # elif (defined __x86_64__ || defined _AMD64_) && defined TCC_TARGET_X86_64
